    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To extract table cells and row structure from a document, I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful OCR (Optical Character Recognition) service provided by AWS. This service can extract text, handwriting, and data from scanned documents. I will write the Python code to call the Amazon Textract API and make the provider identifiable by importing the boto3 library and using the 'textract' client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861048638,
          "start": 1789861046175
